      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ يَدْخُلُ مَكَّةَ فِي اَلسَّنَةِ اَلْمَرَّةَ وَ اَلْمَرَّتَيْنِ وَ اَلثَّلاَثَ كَيْفَ يَصْنَعُ قَالَ «إِذَا دَخَلَ فَلْيَدْخُلْ مُلَبِّياً وَ إِذَا خَرَجَ فَلْيَخْرُجْ مُحِلاًّ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2754 - Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated from Ali ibn Abi Hamzah, who said: I asked Abu Ibrahim (as) about a man who enters Mecca once, twice, or three times in a year. What should he do?\nImam (as) said: \"When he enters, he should do so in the state of ihram, reciting the Talbiyah, and when he leaves, he should exit in the state of non-ihram.\""
        ]
      }
